      "content": "it feels like the \"compromises\" you mentioned basically just mean the big powers get their way anyway while everyone else loses out. isn't it basically true that global governance is just a way to force smaller countries to follow rules that benefit a few powerful states? like, is the whole system just fundamentally rigged against true national sovereignty?",
